enchilada: en0, IO80211 stand-ins and the Apple80211 scan path for wifid (mss=9; Wi-Fi round 6)

mss>=9 only (nothing else changes). sweet_mss_probe() attaches en0 before launchd: an Ethernet
ifnet (IFT_ETHER, subfamily Wi-Fi, no Skywalk nexus, link down, frames dropped and counted) whose
SIOCGIFMEDIA says IEEE 802.11, and below the ADT's "wlan" nub (the platform without one) an
IO80211Controller with IOMACAddress and an IONetworkInterface (SweetWLAN) with IOInterfaceName /
BSD Name en0, IOInterfaceType 6, IOInterfaceUnit 0, IOBuiltin, IOPrimaryInterface and
IO80211InterfaceRole "Infrastructure" (iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetWLAN.cpp). The service has no user
client, so IO80211.framework falls back to SIOCGA80211/SIOCSA80211 on a socket ("Falling back to
IOCTL path", present in 16.7.16's dyld cache); ifioctl() passes them to en0's ioctl
(bsd/dev/sweet_wlan.c): power, card capabilities, op mode, state (INIT), supported channels and
channel info (0267's 38 channels, all passive, DFS 5260-5720), SCAN_REQ (5456 bytes; EBUSY until
the data path is up; answered from 0267's table with APPLE80211_M_SCAN_DONE, a kernel event of
class 6 subclass 1 with "en0" first) and SCAN_RESULT one network per request (1164 bytes: BSSID,
SSID, channel, RSSI, beacon interval, capability, rates, up to 512 bytes of whole IEs, age; EIO
at the end; networks not heard for 60 s are left out). About a joined network: ENXIO; ASSOCIATE:
EOPNOTSUPP. Every request type is logged ("SWEET A80211:", first 4 of each type, then every 100th).
Ported from HakiOS drivers/net/hakios.net.c, drivers/wifi/hakios.apple80211.c and
drivers/wifi/hakios.wlan.cpp (APSL 2.0, (c) 2025-2026 the HakiOS authors; layouts as read from
IO80211.framework of iOS 16.5).
sweet_mss.c: the BSS table keeps whole entries (raw SSID, beacon interval, capability, IEs, last
seen; RSSI of the last frame instead of the maximum) under a mutex; the station vdev uses en0's
address (the ADT wlan local-mac-address, else 02:00:00:53:57:54) instead of the firmware's; at
mss>=9 the stage-6 watch stays open while the WLAN path is alive (no 120 s end, no wlan_mode off;
a failure still ends it, and the wait for wlan_mode off is now relative to when it was sent);
periodic scan lines are printed for the first 8 scans and every 40th. wifid itself only starts
with an ADT "wlan" node (tools/mkadt.py ADT_WLAN=1, logs/wifi/mkadt-adt-wlan.diff) and an IOKit
that quiesces (0269).

